│ patch_name               │ hypercube_shared_params                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The best-performing prior program achieved a combined score of 0.45 by using aggressive   │
│                          │ parameter sharing and a hypercube entanglement pattern, dramatically reducing parameter   │
│                          │ count from 194 to 26 while improving generalization gap from 0.10 to 0.01 and convergence │
│                          │ speed.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program uses 146 parameters with independent per-qubit gates and a line       │
│                          │ entanglement pattern, leading to worse generalization (gap 0.07) and slower convergence   │
│                          │ (750 steps vs 270).                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ I propose to adapt the best-performer's strategy:                                         │
│                          │ 1. **Parameter sharing**: Replace 24 independent parameters (ry_0..ry_7,                  │
│                          │ rz_pre_0..rz_pre_7, rz_post_0..rz_post_7) with just 3-4 collective parameters. This       │
│                          │ dramatically improves parameter efficiency and generalization.                            │
│                          │ 2. **Hypercube entanglement**: Replace the line entanglement (0-1, 1-2, ..., 6-7) with    │
│                          │ three perfect matchings corresponding to the 3D hypercube connectivity. This provides     │
│                          │ balanced all-to-all coupling in fewer gates.                                              │
│                          │ 3. **Output mixing**: Add a collective RX layer after the RY mixer to provide diverse     │
│                          │ unitary coverage for readout conversion.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ These changes will:                                                                       │
│                          │ - Reduce n_params from 146 to ~26 (improving parameter efficiency from 0.01 to 0.03+)     │
│                          │ - Improve generalization (reduce gap from 0.07 to near 0.01)                              │
│                          │ - Speed up convergence (reduce from 750 to ~300 steps)                                    │
│                          │ - Maintain or improve accuracy by leveraging the proven architecture                      │
